    "body": "Problem:\n- `CTRL-W s` at start of line is a word (or h3), not a keycode.\n- `STARTING MACVIM FROM A TERMINAL` is not a h3.\n\nSolution:\n- Try `keycode` before `uppercase_name` at start of line.\n- Match single-char \"words\" after the first (multi-char) word of\n  `uppercase_name`.\n  - Limitation: a single-char FIRST word (\"A TAGS BROWSER\", \"1\n    INTRODUCTION\") is still not h3. A line-start single-char token\n    conflicts with `word`, so treesitter drops `word` from the\n    error-recovery lexer, which breaks recovery (see the \"NOT a taglink\"\n    test).\n\nfix #98\nfix #111\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-14T23:09:11Z",
